  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let $a=4i+2j-k$ and $b=2i+2j-k.$ Find $a\\times b.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2)i-(4\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2)j+(4\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =(-2+2)i-(-4+2)j+(8-4)k \\\\  & =2j+4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
